sts{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/580979383","html_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/3482#issuecomment-580979383","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/3482","id":580979383,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU4MDk3OTM4Mw==","user":{"login":"jaki","id":16715704,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzE1NzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16715704?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki","html_url":"https://github.com/jaki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-02-01T02:06:52Z","updated_at":"2020-02-01T02:06:52Z","body":"I had discovered a potential lead on the issue by dumping out the contents of the intents DB.  Here is the patch that I used:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndiff --git i/src/yb/docdb/ql_rocksdb_storage.cc w/src/yb/docdb/ql_rocksdb_storage.cc\r\nindex b278ae2af..2cb995ad8 100644\r\n--- i/src/yb/docdb/ql_rocksdb_storage.cc\r\n+++ w/src/yb/docdb/ql_rocksdb_storage.cc\r\n@@ -108,6 +108,7 @@ Status QLRocksDBStorage::GetIterator(const PgsqlReadRequestPB& request,\r\n                                      const ReadHybridTime& read_time,\r\n                                      common::YQLRowwiseIteratorIf::UniPtr* iter) const {\r\n   std::unique_ptr<DocRowwiseIterator> doc_iter;\r\n+  LOG(WARNING) << DocDBDebugDumpToStr(doc_db_.intents, StorageDbType::kIntents);\r\n\r\n   // Populate dockey from QL key columns.\r\n   auto hash_code = request.has_hash_code() ?\r\n```\r\n\r\nI proceeded to run the above queries again, with slightly different numbers.  Here are the outputs of the dumps for a non-colocated table and a colocated table:\r\n\r\nNon-colocated:\r\n\r\n```\r\nSubDocKey(DocKey([], []), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516311591879 w: 2 } -> TransactionId(2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab) none\r\nSubDocKey(DocKey([], []), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516308005365 w: 2 } -> TransactionId(2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab) none\r\nSubDocKey(DocKey([], [3]), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516308005365 w: 1 } -> TransactionId(2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab) none\r\nSubDocKey(DocKey([], [3]), [SystemColumnId(0)]) [kStrongRead, kStrongWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516308005365 } -> TransactionId(2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab) WriteId(0) null\r\nSubDocKey(DocKey([], [11]), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516311591879 w: 1 } -> TransactionId(2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab) none\r\nSubDocKey(DocKey([], [11]), [SystemColumnId(0)]) [kStrongRead, kStrongWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516311591879 } -> TransactionId(2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab) WriteId(1) null\r\nTXN META 2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab -> { transaction_id: 2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab isolation: 1 status_tablet: 07e952b7d5d24c9e98e4e56d704b860d priority: 165665571155396771 start_time: { physical: 1580516301677013 } }\r\nTXN REV 2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab HT{ physical: 1580516308005365 } -> SubDocKey(DocKey([], [3]), [SystemColumnId(0)]) [kStrongRead, kStrongWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516308005365 }\r\nTXN REV 2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab HT{ physical: 1580516308005365 w: 1 } -> SubDocKey(DocKey([], [3]), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516308005365 w: 1 }\r\nTXN REV 2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab HT{ physical: 1580516308005365 w: 2 } -> SubDocKey(DocKey([], []), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516308005365 w: 2 }\r\nTXN REV 2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab HT{ physical: 1580516311591879 } -> SubDocKey(DocKey([], [11]), [SystemColumnId(0)]) [kStrongRead, kStrongWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516311591879 }\r\nTXN REV 2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab HT{ physical: 1580516311591879 w: 1 } -> SubDocKey(DocKey([], [11]), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516311591879 w: 1 }\r\nTXN REV 2ed3c9f4-8c46-4d60-93d6-a425da41b4ab HT{ physical: 1580516311591879 w: 2 } -> SubDocKey(DocKey([], []), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516311591879 w: 2 }\r\n```\r\n\r\nColocated:\r\n\r\n```\r\nTXN META 86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1 -> { transaction_id: 86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1 isolation: 1 status_tablet: 460578f0cd34485e95475cbd9411c2e1 priority: 17135805243043803351 start_time: { physical: 1580516394100926 } }\r\nTXN REV 86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1 HT{ physical: 1580516398851002 } -> SubDocKey(DocKey(PgTableId=16390, [], [3]), [SystemColumnId(0)]) [kStrongRead, kStrongWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516398851002 }\r\nTXN REV 86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1 HT{ physical: 1580516398851002 w: 1 } -> SubDocKey(DocKey(PgTableId=16390, [], [3]), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516398851002 w: 1 }\r\nTXN REV 86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1 HT{ physical: 1580516398851002 w: 2 } -> SubDocKey(DocKey(PgTableId=16390, [], []), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516398851002 w: 2 }\r\nTXN REV 86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1 HT{ physical: 1580516403637321 } -> SubDocKey(DocKey(PgTableId=16390, [], [11]), [SystemColumnId(0)]) [kStrongRead, kStrongWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516403637321 }\r\nTXN REV 86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1 HT{ physical: 1580516403637321 w: 1 } -> SubDocKey(DocKey(PgTableId=16390, [], [11]), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516403637321 w: 1 }\r\nTXN REV 86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1 HT{ physical: 1580516403637321 w: 2 } -> SubDocKey(DocKey(PgTableId=16390, [], []), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516403637321 w: 2 }\r\nSubDocKey(DocKey(PgTableId=16390, [], []), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516403637321 w: 2 } -> TransactionId(86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1) none\r\nSubDocKey(DocKey(PgTableId=16390, [], []), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516398851002 w: 2 } -> TransactionId(86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1) none\r\nSubDocKey(DocKey(PgTableId=16390, [], [3]), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516398851002 w: 1 } -> TransactionId(86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1) none\r\nSubDocKey(DocKey(PgTableId=16390, [], [3]), [SystemColumnId(0)]) [kStrongRead, kStrongWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516398851002 } -> TransactionId(86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1) WriteId(0) null\r\nSubDocKey(DocKey(PgTableId=16390, [], [11]), []) [kWeakRead, kWeakWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516403637321 w: 1 } -> TransactionId(86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1) none\r\nSubDocKey(DocKey(PgTableId=16390, [], [11]), [SystemColumnId(0)]) [kStrongRead, kStrongWrite] HT{ physical: 1580516403637321 } -> TransactionId(86db9cce-eb06-4993-b0fc-c34139a3f3a1) WriteId(1) null\r\n```\r\n\r\nI realized that the `TXN META` and `TXN REV` records sort earlier than the intent key records for colocated tables.  This makes sense because the value type `kPgTableOid` (currently ASCII `z`) is higher than the value type `kTransactionId` (currently ASCII `x`).\r\n\r\nWhile I don't know how that ties to this issue, moving the `kPgTableOid` to a lower value type causes this issue to get resolved.  The implication of this is that other records whose keys start with value types higher than `kTransactionId` may have this issue.  When colocated tables used to use `kTableId` (currently ASCII `y`) before issue #3365 was closed, this was a problem, and that makes sense.  @mbautin pointed out that `kNullHigh` is also susceptible to this, and he helped me come up with a repro which I will provide in a new comment.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/580979383/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jaki","id":16715704,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzE1NzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16715704?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki","html_url":"https://github.com/jaki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":2999011990,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50Mjk5OTAxMTk5MA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/events/2999011990","actor":{"login":"mbautin","id":552936,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MjkzNg==","avatar_u